    "summary": "Added src/daemon/threads/indexing-block.ts. createIndexingBlock() creates the shared block. IndexingBlock has two shared flags, codeBusy (the index lane has a job running or queued) and stopping, plus waitForCodeIdle, which waits without blocking on a version word with a keep-alive timer. IndexQueue takes optional { indexingBlock, publishLane, sweepProgress }. At every lane change it writes codeBusy and publishes that lane's depth and processing state; the summary lane also carries the sweep from sweepProgress, and lanesChanged() republishes it. stop() sets stopping. New pause()/resume() stop both lanes from taking new jobs; pause() resolves once nothing is in flight, and stop() also releases paused loops. Lane order, the summary yield and stop/drain are unchanged, and summary-lane jobs can go to another thread through the existing processor argument without any change. Design note: the queue is the single publisher of both lanes, so a separate sweep publisher can never clear the summary lane's state; the summary worker's sweep progress reaches the board through sweepProgress. Existing queue suites pass.",
